I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   WARN cgroup-limit: the container's memory limit is 48.00 GiB and the process pins 41.12 GiB
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: pinned memory counts against the limit and cannot be reclaimed; what is left is all the page cache and the process's own allocations get before the OOM killer
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: raise the container's memory limit or lower the pools
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   note experts-from-host: 7.98 GiB of weights a rank live in the pinned host pool and cross PCIe when they are used
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: a prefill step streams every routed layer's pooled experts onto the card, so its speed is bounded by the link; decode reads the ones it routes to
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: more VRAM for the experts: a shorter --max-model-len or fewer --max-num-seqs, --embedding-placement ram, --kv-cache-dtype i8, or more cards (--tp)
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   note link-capped: card 0000:0a:00.0 (rank 0): the card's link is 32.0 GT/s x16 at most, and 0000:00:03.1 above it is 16.0 GT/s x8 at most
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: the host side of the link bounds what the card can move to and from host memory: streamed experts, the host pool and the all-reduce when it goes through host memory
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: a slot with the card's full width and speed (the board manual says which slots share lanes), or no riser; nothing to do if the board has no faster slot
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   note link-capped: card 0000:0d:00.0 (rank 1): the card's link is 32.0 GT/s x16 at most, and 0000:00:03.2 above it is 16.0 GT/s x8 at most
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: the host side of the link bounds what the card can move to and from host memory: streamed experts, the host pool and the all-reduce when it goes through host memory
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: a slot with the card's full width and speed (the board manual says which slots share lanes), or no riser; nothing to do if the board has no faster slot
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   note memlock-limited: RLIMIT_MEMLOCK is 8.00 MiB and the n-gram table is read from the container on disk
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: a locked copy of the table in RAM is one of the faster tiers, and the memlock limit is one of the things that keeps --ngram-placement auto off it
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: Docker: ulimits memlock -1 (--ulimit memlock=-1); systemd: LimitMEMLOCK=infinity
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]   note cpu-governor: the CPU governor is powersave with energy preference balance_performance
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        why: the host side of a step -- scheduling, sampling, the n-gram gather, launch bookkeeping -- is single-threaded per rank, and a core that ramps slowly shows as host gap between steps
I[qwen3.8-flash-next]        fix: cpupower frequency-set -g performance, or echo performance | sudo tee /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/energy_performance_preference
